                     # Not a loading defect: printed recipe read variant=ortholarge and the curve climbed
                     # 0.7524 -> 0.8452 monotonically; a mis-converted trunk probes at chance.
                     # THIS DECLINE IS THE SEAT DECISION ONLY. It does NOT close the in-domain trunk
                     # lane: ortho_dense moves trunk size (86M -> 303M) and continuation corpus together
                     # against its control, and v3large_dense (running, ~05:00Z 2026-09-02) is the
                     # subtraction that separates them. Re-open by that arm's number, not by this one.

v3large_dense_s2026  # DECLINED AS A SEAT, 2026-09-02. Greedy seat value -0.0012 against the champion
                     # seating -- below the 0.0015 the board can resolve and on the wrong side of zero.
                     # It is the SUBTRACTION arm the ortho_dense decline above asked for: trunk size moves
                     # (86M -> 303M) with the continuation corpus held OUT, and the seat still does not
                     # pay. Read together, the two say the in-domain continuation was not what cost
                     # ortho_dense its -0.0050; the trunk size on this pool is. Re-open only with a
                     # trunk from a DIFFERENT family (RadImageNet DenseNet, supervised ImageNet
                     # VGG/ResNet), never with another DINOv3 size.
                     #
                     # THE FROZEN PROBE SETTLES IT, and it is stronger evidence than either fitted arm
                     # above, because a frozen read removes the recipe from the question entirely. One
                     # run, matched flags, n=909: dinov2-large 0.7852, v3large 0.7446, ortholarge 0.7387.
                     # ortho - v3large = -0.0059 against its OWN control, the weights it continues from,
                     # with the 1.25M-knee corpus the only free variable. That is ortho_probe.sh's
                     # pre-registered REVERSED branch: the continuation COSTS signal, the catastrophic-
                     # forgetting shape Ilse et al. report for RAD-DINO on out-of-domain VinDR. And
                     # v3large itself sits 0.0406 under dinov2-large, so the family was already the
                     # weaker one before the continuation subtracted from it. Together these mean 0.8452
                     # needs no recipe excuse: the features are absent, not mis-fitted. The suspicion
                     # that a big trunk was starved by an 86M-tuned recipe is RETIRED for this trunk.
                     #
                     # ANSWERED 2026-09-03, and the probe leg above is WITHDRAWN AT ITS SOURCE. The
                     # 0.7387 / 0.7446 pair was read at feature_probe's SHARED ridge penalty, the defect
                     # knee-x4yx filed: trunk feature magnitudes differ ~17x, so one penalty cannot be
                     # fair to two trunks. Re-read at the penalty each trunk is entitled to (nested
                     # split, n=909): ortholarge 0.8249, v3large 0.8046 — +0.0203 at focal and +0.0202
                     # at mean. The sign REVERSES against what this entry recorded.
                     # The FITTED holdouts for that same pair are v3large 0.8258 and ortholarge 0.8452:
                     # +0.0194, three times the 0.0062 floor, trunk size held at 303M and only --variant
                     # differing (identical 12 slices / 224 px / band 0.2-0.8 / 4e-5 / 12 epochs, both
                     # converged at 13). So the corrected probe and the fitted arm AGREE to 0.001 on a
                     # +0.020 in-domain continuation gain, measured by two independent instruments.
                     # The frozen-versus-fitted caution stands separately and is NOT what happened here:
                     # radnet121 probes 0.8197 at its OWN penalty and still served 0.6716 fitted, so the
                     # probe is sound for one trunk and inverted for the other. Kimi has that as Q-CV.
                     # The other leg reads v3large's GREEDY SEAT VALUE (-0.0012) as the subtraction,
                     # but seat value is measured inside a 100% DINOv2 pool where any ViT-L is redundant
                     # with nothing, and solo quality is a different question. These two entries remain
                     # correct AS SEAT DECISIONS. What is withdrawn is the last three lines above: the
                     # features are not shown to be absent, and the recipe suspicion is NOT retired.
                     # `ortho_stack` (knee-b7a50) puts ortholarge on band_dense's full recipe — the same
                     # unit step base224 -> band_dense that paid +0.0069 on the ViT-B — and answers it by
                     # measurement. This is not a re-open on trunk SIZE, which line 195 forbids: size is
                     # fixed on both sides of the +0.0194 and the continuation corpus is the free term.

errors_dense_s2026   # DECLINED AS A SEAT, 2026-09-02. Greedy seat value -0.0010, inside the noise band
                     # and negative. The label-error-flagged corpus changes WHAT A MEMBER SEES, which is
                     # one of the two axes the board still calls open, so the decline is about this
                     # member and not about the axis: the dense trunk it was fitted on is the pool's own
                     # monoculture, so a corpus change here is measured against six members that already
                     # saw the same pixels. errors_v3small (running, finishes ~08:05Z 2026-09-02) asks
                     # the same corpus question on a trunk the pool does not hold, and THAT is the arm
                     # this decline defers to.

errors_v3small_s2026 # DECLINED AS A SEAT, 2026-09-02. Best 0.8280 at epoch 6, CONVERGED (patience
                     # fired; convergence_check reads it converged, not truncated, so the number is a
                     # decision and not a floor). That is 0.0298 under band_dense 0.8578 and 0.0241
                     # under the 0.8521 non-DINOv2 seat bar, so it seats nothing and no greedy seat
                     # trial is owed.
                     # IT IS THE ARM errors_dense's DECLINE DEFERRED TO, and it answers that deferral
                     # in the negative. errors_dense asked the label-error-corpus question on the
                     # pool's own dense monoculture and read -0.0010; this asked it on a trunk the pool
                     # does NOT hold, so a corpus effect could not hide behind six members that saw the
                     # same pixels. It did not appear. The label-error-flagged corpus is now measured
                     # on two trunks, one inside the monoculture and one outside it, and neither pays.
                     # WHAT IT DOES NOT CLOSE: v3small is the weaker half of a family whose LARGE member
                     # probes 0.0406 under dinov2-large (see the ortho_dense decline above), so this is
                     # a corpus reading taken on a trunk that was carrying a handicap into it. It closes
                     # the label-error corpus as a SEAT lever; it does not price the corpus on a trunk
                     # that is competitive to begin with.

# ramp_dense_gate.pt — RETIRED 2026-09-03, and the entry is kept as a comment because a decline that is
#   answered is worth more than one that is deleted. It refused the member on its LEVER reading: 0.8578 at
#   peak epoch 7 against calib_dense_hold_s2026 0.8634 on the same 909-study holdout, -0.0056, inside the
#   0.0062 floor and pointing DOWN.
#
#   WHAT ANSWERED IT is not a number, it is a distinction the roster already makes twice. On 2026-09-02
#   both siblings — certainty_ramp 0.8584 and disagreed_ramp 0.8574 — were seated with that same negative
#   control delta written into their roster notes, on the explicit ground that what seats is the CHECKPOINT
#   and what closed is the LEVER. ramp_dense_gate sits at 0.8578, between the two, clearing the 0.8459
#   merit bar and the 0.8521 non-DINOv2 bar. Declining the middle member of three on a delta the outer two
#   were seated despite is not a policy, it is an inconsistency, and it left the member both packaged and
#   declined with every gate green until roster_check reached the contradiction.
#
#   THE LEVER VERDICT SURVIVES INTACT and did not move one inch: three converged ramp arms spanning
#   0.8574-0.8584 against a 0.8634 control read DOWN as a family, the ramp does not pay at this operating
#   point, and it is re-opened only where supervision is thin — the three extreme-UNK labels (Synovitis
#   84.2%, Fracture 56.4%, Baker's 45.9%) and not all twelve, answered with a per-label run. That clause is
#   live and lives in certainty_ramp's roster note and in knee-fxgm.
ortho_lpft_head.pt          # 0.7537 peak e11 (12 of 12, CONVERGED) — stage ONE of the OrthoDiffusion LP-FT
                            # pair (knee-6hfi): the ortholarge trunk FROZEN, head-only, unfreeze_last 0. It
                            # exists to produce a warm start for stage two, never a seat, which is the same
                            # role swin_distill_pre was declined in. The number is still a real read and the
                            # one this arm was armed for: a frozen OrthoDiffusion trunk carries 0.7537 against
                            # base224's 0.8509 on the same 909-study holdout, i.e. -0.097. Stage two
                            # (ortho_lpft_s2026, unfreeze_last 6, whole stack) is what prices the trunk;
                            # re-open on THAT number, never on this one.

mrnet_warm_s2026.pt         # DECLINED as a seat, checkpoint kept. 0.8487 peak e6, CONVERGED (12 of 12; the one_cycle anneal loses 0.004 rather than
  gaining, so e6 is the recipe's ceiling and not a floor). THE PROJECT'S FIRST EXTERNAL-CORPUS MEMBER:
  trunk warm-started from mrnet_acl_pretrain_s2026 (its epoch 7, 225 tensors, 11 head tensors left cold),
  pretrained on MRNet knee MRI. Rule 2.6 permits it; the CC/RUA copyright question is knee-ib4t and is
  about redistribution, not about training here. It was ROSTERED on 2026-09-03 as a hypothesis about
  diversity, with the line saying in writing that the seat was settled by a vote_ceiling reading and not
  by that line. This is that reading, and it declines it.

  THE SEAT IS WORTH ZERO, measured three ways on the twinfive_v1 pool - the fold-0 five, the only
  scoreable roster this project still has, since the champion's six are all --fold -1 and unscoreable by
  construction. Both arms use the SAME pool, so the delta is legitimate; only an absolute number would
  cross the --fold -1 line.
    vote_ceiling, LogitAverage, honest split-half:  5 members 0.8706 -> 6 members 0.8705  (-0.0001)
    seat_value --against twinfive_v1, added sixth:  -0.0000, band [-0.0010, +0.0009]
    seat_value, best SWAP (for lr4e-5_ws_s2026):    +0.0004, against BOARD_RESOLVABLE 0.0040

  AND THE DECORRELATION IS REAL, WHICH IS WHY THIS IS A DECLINE AND NOT A NULL. MemberDistance puts its
  nearest neighbour at 0.8892, inside the roster's own nearest spread (0.8696 to 0.8972), so it is not a
  twin; its MEAN correlation of 0.8552 is lower than any seated member's NEAREST, making it the most
  globally distant candidate this pool has been offered. It still buys 0.0000. So knee-nj4l's monoculture
  claim is NOT refuted here - it is untested by this member. Corpus distance on the SAME lens (a DINOv2
  trunk warm-started elsewhere) produces measurable ordering distance and zero seat value. What remains
  unmeasured is ARCHITECTURE distance, which is what ortho_pool_read is on the card for.

  THE SPECIALIST RESCUE WAS TRIED AND FAILED. MRNet's pretraining task is ACL tear, and mrnet leads the
  whole pool on ACL solo: 0.8840 against depth_regions_narrow 0.8737, calib_span 0.8706, lr4e-5_ws 0.8706
  - plus 0.0103 on the one label its corpus was built for, which is exactly the shape a specialist has.
  Its 0.8487 mean is dragged down elsewhere (Fracture 0.7954 against 0.8253, PF OA 0.8192), and a
  per-label rank average charges that weakness eleven times against one strength. So the obvious rescue
  is to seat it on ACL only. Measured, per label, LogitAverage over the same five vs the same six:
    ACL +0.0014   MCL +0.0027   MedMen +0.0008   LatMen +0.0003   MedOA -0.0008   LatOA +0.0017
    PFOA -0.0027  Effusion +0.0006  Synovitis -0.0014  Baker's -0.0021  Contusion +0.0020  Fracture -0.0019
  Seven up, five down, largest move 0.0027, mean +0.0000. The ACL specialism does not survive into the
  pool because the pool is ALREADY at 0.9011 on ACL - well above mrnet's 0.8840 solo. A member cannot
  lift a label it is worse at than the vote already is.

  RE-OPEN BY, and not by re-quoting 0.8487: (a) an external-corpus member whose TRUNK differs, not whose
  corpus does - the axis this one holds fixed; (b) a per-label reading on a label where the POOL is weak
  and the external corpus is strong, which ACL is not (MCL 0.8114 and Lateral OA 0.8249 are the pool's
  two weakest, and MRNet supervises neither). The checkpoint is kept; only the seat is refused.

ortho_pool_read.pt  # A PROBE, and it was never a seat candidate. It exists to read one thing: whether
  `ortholarge` - DINOv3-L weights moved by 1.25M knee-MRI slices - carries knee structure a natural-image
  trunk does not. Peak 0.8464 at epoch 8, below both the 0.8492 floor edge and the 0.8521 non-DINOv2 seat
  bar, so it is DIRECTIONAL and nothing more; the reading it was armed for is the LP-FT triple, which is
  still one control short (knee-6hfi, `ortho_fresh_lowlr`).

  IT IS ALSO NOT SHIPPABLE TODAY, for a reason that has nothing to do with the number. `ortholarge`'s
  release licence is unresolved against the fastMRI DSA the continuation corpus may draw on - knee-nxthh,
  and Kimi's Q-CE is outstanding on exactly this. Rostering it would declare shippable a member whose
  right to ship is an open question, which is the failure mode `mount_check` catches one step too late.

  RE-OPEN BY: Q-CE resolving PERMIT, plus a score that clears 0.8521. Either alone is not enough - the
  licence gates the seat and the number gates the merit, and this member currently fails both.

